A MK Studio "starpack" is a Tcl runtime (a "tclkit") with MK Studio's own files appended. Components of that runtime:

  Tcl and Tk            Tcl/Tk license (BSD-style).     https://www.tcl-lang.org/software/tcltk/license.html
                        Included: Tcl and Tk 8.6.3 (Linux, Windows) and 8.6.16 (macOS); Tcl 8.5.17 is used only in tests.
  Metakit and Mk4tcl    MIT-style license.              https://github.com/jcw/metakit  (Jean-Claude Wippler)
                        The database engine and its Tcl binding.
  tclvfs, itcl, tcllib-style helpers
                        the same Tcl/BSD-style licenses as Tcl itself (as built into the tclkit).
  zlib                  zlib license.                   https://zlib.net/zlib_license.html
                        (visible in the binary as "deflate 1.2.8 Copyright 1995-2013 Jean-loup Gailly and Mark Adler"
                        in the 2014 tclkits; 1.3.1 in the macOS kit built in CI)
  tclkit runtime        built by the KitCreator project (Roy Keene) - https://kitcreator.rkeene.org/ ; the prebuilt
                        Linux and Windows runtimes are downloaded from https://tclkits.rkeene.org/ (see
                        tools/fetch-runtimes.sh, which checks their SHA-1). The macOS runtime is compiled in CI from
                        KitCreator.

The Windows installer is built with NSIS (zlib/libpng-style license, https://nsis.sourceforge.io/), which only runs at
build time; its stub is part of the installer.

The installer and the icons are made for MK Studio (tools/make-icons.py) and are covered by LICENSE.

Where a runtime ships its own license files they are inside the starpack (Tcl's "license.terms" in the library
directory). If any attribution here is missing or wrong, please open an issue.
